WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.841
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.111 --> 00:55.076
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:55.160 --> 00:57.120
PREVIOUSLY ON

4
00:57.203 --> 01:00.039
When you save up enough, will you really go to America?

5
01:00.123 --> 01:02.417
I'm going to leave Joseon, no matter what.

6
01:02.500 --> 01:03.710
Who's here?

7
01:03.793 --> 01:07.422
It's the inspector general of the Government-General of Joseon.

8
01:07.505 --> 01:08.548
Nice to meet you.

9
01:08.631 --> 01:12.177
I'm Yoo Philip, Keijo correspondent for the American WWP News Agency.

10
01:12.886 --> 01:14.262
-What's the matter? -My bag…

11
01:14.345 --> 01:16.097
We'll be conducting a brief inspection.

12
01:16.181 --> 01:17.682
Form a single line, everyone!

13
01:21.352 --> 01:22.687
-I'm sorry. -I'm sorry.

14
01:23.271 --> 01:24.689
Someone stole your wallet?

15
01:24.772 --> 01:26.900
Was there something important in it?

16
01:27.567 --> 01:28.401
Not really.

17
01:29.861 --> 01:31.237
Isn't this a pawn ticket?

18
01:31.321 --> 01:32.739
"Sin Tae-jin."

19
01:32.822 --> 01:34.115
The bag…

20
01:34.199 --> 01:35.116
What do we do?

21
01:35.200 --> 01:38.161
Even if the thief finds what's in there,

22
01:39.370 --> 01:42.081
we can only hope nothing goes wrong until after next Thursday.

23
01:42.165 --> 01:42.999
A bullet?

24
01:43.082 --> 01:45.376
I deliberately approached and married

25
01:45.460 --> 01:48.213
an American who knew nothing in Shanghai and came to Gyeongseong

26
01:48.296 --> 01:49.672
to assassinate Sato.

27
01:49.756 --> 01:52.884
Thank you for preparing such a nice meal tonight.

28
01:53.968 --> 01:55.428
I'll give the bullets back.

29
01:55.511 --> 01:56.638
Just give me 60 won.

30
01:56.721 --> 01:58.306
So it's you. The pickpocket.

31
01:58.389 --> 01:59.766
That's all I have now.

32
01:59.849 --> 02:01.976
Wait here quietly, and I'll get the rest later.

33
02:02.060 --> 02:03.478
I didn't expect to see you here.

34
02:03.561 --> 02:04.604
My wallet.

35
02:04.687 --> 02:05.813
I'd like it back.

36
02:07.065 --> 02:10.735
Are you expecting a cake from Itsukoshi Department Store?

37
02:12.362 --> 02:14.113
Make a sound, and you'll die first.

38
02:16.407 --> 02:18.201
Father, stay inside!

39
02:20.620 --> 02:22.830
His name is Keum Seok-jung.

40
02:22.914 --> 02:26.334
I wanted nothing more than to find him and kill him.

41
02:26.417 --> 02:27.961
He's my husband.

42
02:28.044 --> 02:29.629
The protest in this village

43
02:29.712 --> 02:30.922
was all me.

44
02:31.005 --> 02:32.006
Shoot.

45
02:33.132 --> 02:34.342
No!

46
02:36.261 --> 02:38.805
We had our daughter after ten years of marriage,

47
02:38.888 --> 02:40.974
and that's how I lost her.

48
02:41.557 --> 02:44.644
In that moment, when I had to call her something…

49
02:44.727 --> 02:45.728
Keum Seo-hee!

50
02:46.312 --> 02:47.230
Seo-hee

51
02:47.855 --> 02:49.399
was my daughter's name.

52
02:49.482 --> 02:53.319
I'll report to the governor-general that the Gugukdan was behind the attack.

53
02:53.403 --> 02:55.863
They've been a thorn in our side for years.

54
02:55.947 --> 02:57.991
We'll use this chance to wipe them out.

55
03:02.495 --> 03:06.708
There's an opening for an interpreter trainee at the Government-General.

56
03:06.791 --> 03:09.210
I'll send you to America. Work at the Government-General.

57
03:09.294 --> 03:11.045
You want me to be a spy?

58
03:11.129 --> 03:13.965
Infiltrate the Government-General as a spy and work for us.

59
03:14.590 --> 03:17.051
After three months, send me to America.

60
03:17.135 --> 03:21.264
Hideo isn't Sato's real son. Sato adopted a Joseon boy.

61
03:21.347 --> 03:23.474
He graduated from the Imperial Japanese Army Academy

62
03:23.558 --> 03:25.560
and works for the Government-General of Joseon.

63
03:25.643 --> 03:27.312
Keep your guard up around him.

64
03:27.395 --> 03:28.938
Good morning.

65
03:29.022 --> 03:33.526
I'm Keum Seo-hee, the new interpreter trainee assigned here.

66
03:36.029 --> 03:39.032
I don't completely trust her either. And I shouldn't.

67
03:39.115 --> 03:41.200
But Ga-kyung will do fine.

68
03:42.160 --> 03:44.620
-Get the inspector general's schedule. -There.

69
03:44.704 --> 03:47.707
Give it to the man with the lemon in his teacup.

70
03:48.583 --> 03:49.417
Arigato.

71
03:49.500 --> 03:51.961
But she'll definitely put us in danger.

72
04:04.849 --> 04:06.517
That was easy.

73
04:13.316 --> 04:14.233
Freeze.

74
04:15.943 --> 04:17.820
You're a spy, aren't you?

75
04:20.406 --> 04:21.366
Keum Seo-hee.

76
04:22.408 --> 04:23.409
No, I mean,

77
04:23.493 --> 04:24.452
Lee Ga-kyung.

78
05:02.532 --> 05:03.866
Do you know where you are?

79
05:06.077 --> 05:08.830
This is where Josenjings die one by one every single day.

80
05:09.872 --> 05:13.251
It's been over 20 years since Joseon came under Japanese rule,

81
05:13.334 --> 05:17.255
yet Josenjings still can't face reality and keep acting up.

82
05:19.590 --> 05:20.508
Do you get it now?

83
05:21.342 --> 05:23.719
You're at Jongno Police Station.

84
05:27.765 --> 05:30.017
Why… Why am I here?

85
05:32.520 --> 05:33.479
Lee Ga-kyung.

86
05:34.397 --> 05:36.774
A pickpocket from the shantytown in Gyodang-ri.

87
05:37.442 --> 05:39.819
-Gyeongseong Station is your usual turf. -No.

88
05:40.736 --> 05:42.280
I'm…

89
05:42.363 --> 05:45.408
Keum Seo-hee, an interpreter trainee at the Government-General of Joseon.

90
05:45.491 --> 05:48.077
I don't even know who Lee Ga-kyung is.

91
05:49.078 --> 05:50.037
Fine.

92
05:50.746 --> 05:51.873
Whatever your name is.

93
05:55.668 --> 05:58.212
Tell me. Who sent you as a spy?

94
06:02.508 --> 06:04.177
Tell me, who's behind this?

95
06:05.052 --> 06:06.137
I don't know.

96
06:06.220 --> 06:08.473
I really don't!

97
06:12.518 --> 06:14.979
Still going to pretend you don't know?

98
06:15.062 --> 06:16.481
You still don't know?

99
06:16.564 --> 06:17.565
Say it already!

100
06:18.065 --> 06:19.150
I'm not a spy!

101
06:20.109 --> 06:24.489
I told you, I'm an interpreter trainee at the Government-General!

102
06:25.615 --> 06:26.866
Enough.

103
06:33.206 --> 06:34.457
So you will not confess?

104
06:40.505 --> 06:42.965
Fine. Then I'll tell you.

105
06:45.009 --> 06:45.968
Yoo Philip.

106
06:46.594 --> 06:47.553
It's him, isn't it?

107
06:49.847 --> 06:50.723
Or

108
06:51.516 --> 06:52.725
is it his wife?

109
06:58.856 --> 07:01.692
A low-life pickpocket like you wouldn't become a spy for independence.

110
07:03.069 --> 07:03.903
Say it.

111
07:03.986 --> 07:06.614
What were you promised in exchange for being a spy?

112
07:08.449 --> 07:09.283
Speak!

113
07:10.284 --> 07:11.244
Was it money?

114
07:11.327 --> 07:13.496
Tell me who's behind this.

115
07:14.330 --> 07:15.915
Not only will I spare your life,

116
07:15.998 --> 07:18.417
but I'll give you exactly what they promised you.

117
07:21.295 --> 07:22.922
Aren't you afraid of dying?

118
07:23.005 --> 07:27.009
You think taking this to your grave will free Joseon?

119
07:35.101 --> 07:36.561
I'll ask you one last time.

120
07:39.480 --> 07:41.190
Who's behind this?

121
07:50.157 --> 07:51.242
The one behind me is…

122
07:51.325 --> 07:53.536
Yes. Out with it!

123
07:56.080 --> 07:57.206
Joseon.

124
07:59.500 --> 08:00.334
What?

125
08:02.169 --> 08:03.671
I'm not a spy.

126
08:05.256 --> 08:08.968
If anyone stands behind me, it's the 20 million people of Joseon.

127
08:09.051 --> 08:11.387
Independence for Korea!

128
08:11.470 --> 08:12.847
You bitch!

129
08:25.318 --> 08:26.152
You tell me.

130
08:27.445 --> 08:29.196
Who is behind you?

131
08:40.750 --> 08:47.214
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

132
08:47.965 --> 08:50.217
EPISODE 4

133
09:03.689 --> 09:05.858
I knew it had to be you.

134
09:07.151 --> 09:08.986
What on earth are you doing?

135
09:09.070 --> 09:11.572
How could you pull something like this behind my back?

136
09:11.656 --> 09:12.490
I'm sorry.

137
09:14.742 --> 09:17.495
I planned the whole thing. Please forgive me.

138
09:20.456 --> 09:23.751
Didn't you trust me when you made me a spy?

139
09:24.502 --> 09:26.087
Did you think I'd start bawling

140
09:26.170 --> 09:28.422
and confess everything if you put a gun to my head?

141
09:31.384 --> 09:33.135
This is just ridiculous.

142
09:34.261 --> 09:35.471
And listen.

143
09:35.554 --> 09:38.432
If you're going to put on a show, at least do it properly.

144
09:38.933 --> 09:42.645
Did you think that just because you fooled me once, you'd fool me again?

145
09:45.523 --> 09:46.565
You know what?

146
09:47.108 --> 09:49.110
I know a thing or two about Jongno Police Station.

147
09:50.319 --> 09:52.196
In my neighborhood,

148
09:52.279 --> 09:56.283
plenty of people were tortured there and ended up crippled.

149
09:56.951 --> 09:59.745
At Jongno Police Station, if you passed out from the beatings,

150
09:59.829 --> 10:02.915
they'd hang you upside down and pour pepper water up your nose to wake you up.

151
10:02.998 --> 10:04.959
They'd pull out your fingernails and toenails

152
10:05.042 --> 10:08.045
and sear your body with red-hot metal chopsticks.

153
10:08.129 --> 10:11.424
But this place? To call it Jongno Police Station,

154
10:11.507 --> 10:13.718
it's way too simple.

155
10:16.095 --> 10:16.929
Besides…

156
10:25.187 --> 10:28.107
When people lose their tempers, they grab whatever's handy and hit you.

157
10:28.190 --> 10:30.109
But you didn't use that club.

158
10:30.192 --> 10:31.986
I guess you felt bad for me, right?

159
10:33.446 --> 10:34.655
Well…

160
10:35.364 --> 10:36.949
And the sound of the streetcar.

161
10:41.036 --> 10:42.288
In the car,

162
10:42.371 --> 10:45.082
I heard a streetcar passing nearby.

163
10:46.333 --> 10:49.920
But from where you grabbed me, no matter which route you take,

164
10:50.004 --> 10:53.174
we'd never pass a streetcar on the way to Jongno Police Station.

165
10:56.010 --> 10:58.137
And if this really were Jongno Police Station,

166
10:58.220 --> 11:00.681
why would you blindfold me?

167
11:00.765 --> 11:01.807
Why bother?

168
11:04.435 --> 11:06.228
I'm being awfully kind, aren't I?

169
11:06.729 --> 11:09.273
You all tried so hard, I almost feel bad for you.

170
11:09.857 --> 11:11.776
I'm giving you tips so you do better next time.

171
11:13.819 --> 11:16.530
Well then, I'm out.

172
11:17.031 --> 11:19.033
You don't trust me.

173
11:19.116 --> 11:20.826
How am I supposed to trust you

174
11:20.910 --> 11:23.162
and risk my life and work as a spy?

175
11:23.746 --> 11:25.664
So don't think this is unfair.

176
11:26.832 --> 11:28.793
I'll take the advance as payment for the beating.

177
11:33.672 --> 11:36.842
About what I said earlier, "Independence for Korea."

178
11:36.926 --> 11:38.177
Don't read into it.

179
11:39.345 --> 11:40.638
Like I told you,

180
11:40.721 --> 11:41.972
Joseon's independence

181
11:42.056 --> 11:44.266
is none of my concern, and I don't want to get involved.

182
11:46.519 --> 11:47.812
I only said that

183
11:47.895 --> 11:49.897
to get your little play over with.

184
11:52.817 --> 11:54.360
Get your hand off the door.

185
11:56.612 --> 11:59.990
This gun is loaded, and I really will shoot if you open it.

186
12:07.039 --> 12:08.332
Hands off!

187
12:11.502 --> 12:12.378
Put the gun down.

188
12:15.297 --> 12:16.423
Step aside, So-ran.

189
12:17.341 --> 12:18.926
-So-ran! -So-ran.

190
12:22.388 --> 12:23.639
Put the gun down.

191
12:54.295 --> 12:55.379
Seo-hee…

192
12:57.548 --> 12:59.008
was my daughter's name.

193
13:01.427 --> 13:04.096
My daughter, the one killed by the inspector general.

194
13:12.313 --> 13:13.939
Help us. We…

195
13:17.276 --> 13:19.194
I need you.

196
13:32.249 --> 13:35.044
Please don't ever keep anything about her from me again.

197
13:35.961 --> 13:38.172
Were you really going to shoot me?

198
13:39.089 --> 13:42.009
Or was it just part of the act to win her over?

199
13:50.184 --> 13:52.061
You brought up Seo-hee to her.

200
13:52.144 --> 13:53.604
Was it part of your plan too?

201
13:57.191 --> 13:58.567
Don't worry about her.

202
13:59.276 --> 14:02.738
She's desperate to go to America. So she won't betray us easily.

203
14:02.821 --> 14:04.865
That's why she must never find out

204
14:05.950 --> 14:07.701
that there was never any way

205
14:09.078 --> 14:11.163
to get her to America in the first place.

206
14:18.963 --> 14:20.214
Keum Seo-hee!

207
14:22.383 --> 14:23.384
Help me…

208
14:25.678 --> 14:27.054
Seo-hee

209
14:27.137 --> 14:28.806
was my daughter's name.

210
14:31.308 --> 14:34.269
My daughter, the one killed by the inspector general.

211
14:47.241 --> 14:49.827
Oh dear.

212
15:11.140 --> 15:13.225
You don't need to keep warming that up.

213
15:13.809 --> 15:15.394
Winter is almost over anyway.

214
15:16.186 --> 15:18.022
It's still winter in Gyeongseong.

215
15:18.105 --> 15:20.024
It's much colder than Tokyo, you know.

216
15:23.652 --> 15:25.863
What's wrong? Can't you breathe?

217
15:26.864 --> 15:28.657
No, I'm fine…

218
15:28.741 --> 15:30.492
Let's get you to a doctor. I'll call a cab.

219
15:31.076 --> 15:32.369
No, really, I'm fine.

220
15:34.204 --> 15:35.873
It's just a passing spell.

221
15:39.710 --> 15:41.211
All right.

222
15:41.295 --> 15:45.132
If it happens again, you have to go straight to the hospital.

223
15:48.177 --> 15:50.554
Hideo, I'm done writing.

224
15:51.221 --> 15:52.431
All done?

225
15:54.850 --> 15:56.560
It looks really good.

226
15:56.643 --> 15:57.978
-Really? -Yeah.

227
15:58.062 --> 16:00.522
Let's write them ten more times each.

228
16:00.606 --> 16:01.732
Okay.

229
16:04.610 --> 16:05.444
But…

230
16:07.780 --> 16:08.781
You know…

231
16:16.580 --> 16:18.415
Once I learn all the lowercase letters,

232
16:19.041 --> 16:20.793
teach me the Joseon language, please.

233
16:22.795 --> 16:24.004
The Joseon language.

234
16:25.214 --> 16:27.007
Since my mom

235
16:27.758 --> 16:29.510
was a Joseon person…

236
16:31.512 --> 16:32.346
But

237
16:33.222 --> 16:34.890
promise you won't tell Father.

238
16:38.936 --> 16:40.062
Okay.

239
16:41.772 --> 16:43.023
I promise I'll teach you.

240
16:43.107 --> 16:44.191
Okay.

241
16:45.734 --> 16:47.611
What will you teach her?

242
16:48.487 --> 16:49.613
I'll tell you later.

243
16:53.951 --> 16:54.868
Ma'am.

244
16:55.953 --> 16:56.829
By any chance…

245
16:59.206 --> 17:01.125
do you know my mother's Joseon name?

246
17:01.208 --> 17:02.459
Her Joseon name?

247
17:03.669 --> 17:05.587
No, I don't. I've never heard.

248
17:06.380 --> 17:08.257
Why ask all of a sudden?

249
17:09.299 --> 17:10.134
The truth is…

250
17:12.094 --> 17:14.388
I've been looking for her since I returned to Gyeongseong.

251
17:37.411 --> 17:38.954
I'm home.

252
17:40.998 --> 17:42.833
Did you have a good day?

253
18:04.396 --> 18:07.357
I stumbled upon something while packing our things in Tokyo.

254
18:07.983 --> 18:09.985
I think it might help me find my mother.

255
18:11.778 --> 18:12.779
But…

256
18:14.364 --> 18:15.908
please don't let Father know.

257
18:17.576 --> 18:18.410
I won't.

258
18:24.833 --> 18:27.085
Look, I did all ten.

259
18:29.421 --> 18:30.339
What is this?

260
18:30.839 --> 18:31.882
This is…

261
18:32.633 --> 18:33.926
On Kim Gu's orders,

262
18:34.009 --> 18:37.179
Lee Bong-chang attempted to assassinate His Majesty the Emperor in Tokyo.

263
18:37.262 --> 18:40.140
That bombing attempt happened only three months ago.

264
18:42.100 --> 18:43.310
And not long ago,

265
18:43.936 --> 18:46.563
the subversive group captured in Hwanghae Province

266
18:46.647 --> 18:50.901
was sent by the self-proclaimed government in Shanghai to kill the governor-general.

267
18:52.819 --> 18:54.154
You know that, don't you?

268
18:55.239 --> 18:56.073
Yes, sir.

269
18:56.156 --> 18:58.659
Even the Western press

270
18:59.660 --> 19:01.245
calls them "terrorists."

271
19:01.828 --> 19:04.039
The whole world sees them for what they are,

272
19:04.122 --> 19:08.210
yet we can't even catch one fugitive right under our noses.

273
19:09.503 --> 19:11.880
Does that make sense to you?

274
19:13.590 --> 19:14.800
I have no excuse, sir.

275
19:15.926 --> 19:20.138
The fugitive from Yoo Philip's place is still at large,

276
19:21.056 --> 19:22.599
but we've raided

277
19:22.683 --> 19:25.102
several independence group bases and arrested many of them.

278
19:25.852 --> 19:28.647
We're wringing information from those already in custody.

279
19:28.730 --> 19:29.940
However,

280
19:30.774 --> 19:34.361
they're a tough bunch. Keeping silent is what they do best.

281
19:35.279 --> 19:36.280
I'm sorry, sir.

282
19:39.324 --> 19:41.076
It's not that they're tough.

283
19:43.161 --> 19:44.705
You're just too soft.

284
19:46.873 --> 19:48.125
Forgive me, sir!

285
19:50.252 --> 19:53.714
You've lived in Joseon for 20 years,

286
19:55.465 --> 19:57.801
but you have yet to learn what Joseon people are like.

287
19:59.511 --> 20:00.470
Forgive me, sir.

288
20:00.554 --> 20:02.681
Have you forgotten what happened to them

289
20:02.764 --> 20:05.100
when they cried for independence back in 1919?

290
20:07.853 --> 20:09.855
Even after seeing all that bloodshed,

291
20:11.064 --> 20:14.860
they're still carrying on with their stupid independence movement.

292
20:15.652 --> 20:17.029
They just won't give it up.

293
20:18.488 --> 20:19.781
Why do you think that is?

294
20:21.908 --> 20:24.328
Because there's something in them that can't be broken

295
20:25.662 --> 20:27.914
by swords, guns, and torture.

296
20:28.915 --> 20:31.501
And what is that, sir?

297
20:33.503 --> 20:34.421
Hope.

298
20:35.756 --> 20:37.507
The delusional hope

299
20:38.383 --> 20:40.218
that independence will come someday.

300
20:41.636 --> 20:44.139
A bullet can kill a man, and that's the end of his life.

301
20:45.307 --> 20:47.601
But hope is passed down to the next generation.

302
20:50.020 --> 20:53.982
So we have to crush it completely.

303
20:54.524 --> 20:56.818
Right down to the very roots. All of it.

304
20:58.987 --> 21:01.198
Despite 20 years of our enlightenment,

305
21:01.740 --> 21:04.493
they're still uncivilized savages.

306
21:05.202 --> 21:07.120
By doing so, they'll know their place

307
21:07.204 --> 21:09.373
and come under our civilized rule.

308
21:09.456 --> 21:12.000
Indeed, sir.

309
21:14.294 --> 21:15.420
And yet,

310
21:16.505 --> 21:19.341
those pampered elites back in Tokyo

311
21:19.841 --> 21:21.093
sit in luxury

312
21:21.176 --> 21:24.179
debating the enlightenment and peace of Joseon.

313
21:28.308 --> 21:31.019
Even though they've never even set foot on this soil.

314
21:34.606 --> 21:37.150
I was born and raised in Joseon.

315
21:38.235 --> 21:42.114
No one knows the Joseon people better than I do.

316
21:44.658 --> 21:47.285
The future of Joseon will be shaped

317
21:47.911 --> 21:50.539
by my hands right here.

318
21:52.874 --> 21:55.127
Yes, sir! You have my absolute loyalty!

319
22:08.598 --> 22:10.267
We should head out separately.

320
22:23.780 --> 22:24.698
I'm off.

321
22:36.084 --> 22:36.960
Damn it.

322
22:38.003 --> 22:38.920
Lee Ga-kyung.

323
22:43.800 --> 22:44.759
Who?

324
22:45.802 --> 22:46.970
I'm Keum Seo-hee.

325
22:49.055 --> 22:50.098
I'm warning you.

326
22:50.182 --> 22:53.602
If you put her in danger, you won't be safe either.

327
22:57.814 --> 23:01.359
So your warning was about her, not the Gugukdan?

328
23:08.533 --> 23:10.577
Next time, I'm keeping it.

329
23:40.106 --> 23:42.234
He was a Joseon orphan?

330
23:43.652 --> 23:45.695
That's why he said that…

331
23:45.779 --> 23:48.657
I was impressed by your pickpocketing skills.

332
23:48.740 --> 23:50.575
I was quite hopeless myself.

333
23:55.038 --> 23:55.872
Ms. Keum.

334
23:56.456 --> 23:57.290
Yes?

335
23:57.374 --> 23:59.417
Your job description doesn't include cleaning.

336
23:59.501 --> 24:01.294
You don't give me any work, so I was bored.

337
24:01.378 --> 24:03.296
How dare I order someone like you around?

338
24:03.880 --> 24:06.174
If you insist on cleaning, that's up to you.

339
24:06.258 --> 24:08.718
Make sure he knows I didn't force you to do it

340
24:08.802 --> 24:10.011
to avoid any misunderstanding.

341
24:10.095 --> 24:11.471
Will do.

342
24:14.891 --> 24:16.643
When will you give me the pawn ticket back?

343
24:18.562 --> 24:20.689
Why bring up something we already settled?

344
24:21.940 --> 24:24.609
But you don't need the pawn ticket

345
24:24.693 --> 24:26.444
until you find the pawnshop anyway.

346
24:29.155 --> 24:31.116
So will you give it back once I find the pawnshop?

347
24:31.199 --> 24:32.617
Yes, absolutely.

348
24:32.701 --> 24:33.868
You promise?

349
24:33.952 --> 24:35.704
I promise.

350
24:35.787 --> 24:36.663
You have my word.

351
24:41.209 --> 24:42.168
Yes, this is Sato.

352
24:43.086 --> 24:45.046
Oh, the English dictionary?

353
24:45.130 --> 24:46.631
Yes, I'll bring it right away.

354
24:48.550 --> 24:49.384
Ms. Keum.

355
24:50.218 --> 24:52.178
-Yes? -Take this here.

356
24:53.888 --> 24:56.391
Don't take the elevator. Use the stairs.

357
24:56.474 --> 24:57.767
I don't use the elevator myself.

358
24:57.851 --> 25:02.105
Sure. A mere interpreter trainee shouldn't use the elevator meant for the higher-ups.

359
25:03.523 --> 25:06.818
You're the inspector general's son and even you can't ride it?

360
25:07.402 --> 25:09.195
I said I don't take it. I never said I can't.

361
25:13.408 --> 25:15.785
PUBLICATIONS DIVISION ISHIKAWA

362
25:17.829 --> 25:19.372
Excuse me, sir.

363
25:19.456 --> 25:21.499
You're still here?

364
25:21.583 --> 25:23.793
Where did you say I should deliver this?

365
25:23.877 --> 25:25.003
It's written right there.

366
25:28.882 --> 25:29.716
What is it?

367
25:31.009 --> 25:31.968
It's just that…

368
25:33.970 --> 25:36.097
I can't read Chinese characters very well.

369
25:36.890 --> 25:37.724
What?

370
25:39.059 --> 25:41.478
I never got to go to school, so…

371
25:42.270 --> 25:45.607
I can speak just fine, but reading and writing are a bit hard.

372
25:46.775 --> 25:47.609
Give it to me.

373
25:52.322 --> 25:54.908
In Joseon, you say Publications Division. In the national language…

374
25:56.576 --> 25:57.702
In Japanese,

375
25:57.786 --> 26:00.914
it's read "henshuuka."

376
26:03.500 --> 26:05.835
-And his name is-- -Mr. Ishikawa.

377
26:06.378 --> 26:09.547
Ishikawa is a pretty common surname.

378
26:10.590 --> 26:12.634
I know the basic characters.

379
26:13.843 --> 26:15.762
Fine, if you say so.

380
26:20.475 --> 26:21.726
It's on the fourth floor.

381
26:22.519 --> 26:23.395
Okay.

382
26:25.605 --> 26:26.898
Did you hurt your leg?

383
26:27.774 --> 26:30.485
I won't use the elevator. Don't worry.

384
26:36.491 --> 26:37.826
I'll be on my way.

385
26:37.909 --> 26:44.708
PUBLICATIONS DIVISION

386
27:19.576 --> 27:21.953
What are you doing here?

387
27:26.374 --> 27:28.835
Making sure I don't use the elevator?

388
27:29.586 --> 27:30.670
What?

389
27:32.046 --> 27:32.881
Unbelievable.

390
27:48.146 --> 27:48.980
Hold onto me.

391
27:55.153 --> 27:56.654
That's okay.

392
27:56.738 --> 27:57.697
Are you sure?

393
27:59.282 --> 28:00.116
Yes.

394
28:07.749 --> 28:08.917
Help me.

395
28:10.460 --> 28:12.170
Help me!

396
28:25.683 --> 28:28.728
Don't you know the magic word "please"?

397
28:29.646 --> 28:30.772
Forget it!

398
28:40.448 --> 28:43.451
Sir, please let me use the elevator just this once.

399
28:43.535 --> 28:46.204
I can ride it if I'm with you, right?

400
28:46.287 --> 28:49.874
It hurts too much. I can't even walk.

401
29:05.348 --> 29:07.517
Let's make our way down first.

402
29:26.077 --> 29:27.078
Where are you going?

403
29:27.829 --> 29:29.789
The elevator's that way.

404
29:30.623 --> 29:32.292
You aren't allowed to use the elevator.

405
29:32.876 --> 29:35.920
Even if I'm with you, I can't?

406
29:39.841 --> 29:40.925
It's because you are…

407
29:43.094 --> 29:44.512
a Joseon person.

408
29:56.691 --> 29:58.359
Let's go down to the first floor.

409
29:59.444 --> 30:01.195
We're going out for work.

410
30:03.406 --> 30:04.490
Outside?

411
30:12.665 --> 30:13.917
Why aren't you coming?

412
30:14.000 --> 30:14.876
What?

413
30:17.003 --> 30:17.837
I'm coming.

414
30:21.633 --> 30:23.343
HANSEONG MEDICINE CLINIC

415
30:23.968 --> 30:25.845
Her right ankle is a little swollen.

416
30:26.930 --> 30:28.556
Please come this way.

417
30:32.018 --> 30:32.852
Let's go.

418
30:33.561 --> 30:34.395
Okay.

419
30:48.284 --> 30:49.661
Why are you standing there?

420
30:50.161 --> 30:51.579
Either sit down or lie down.

421
30:54.123 --> 30:56.167
Are you worried about the bill?

422
30:56.751 --> 30:59.629
I suppose you've already spent all the money in my wallet.

423
30:59.712 --> 31:01.631
No, that's not it.

424
31:03.758 --> 31:04.842
The thing is

425
31:05.593 --> 31:08.596
I've never been to a clinic to get treated before.

426
31:12.100 --> 31:13.017
My goodness.

427
31:14.727 --> 31:15.603
All right.

428
31:17.939 --> 31:19.190
What brings you in today?

429
31:30.159 --> 31:32.120
Her right ankle is quite swollen.

430
31:33.955 --> 31:34.956
Right.

431
31:35.540 --> 31:37.208
I sprained my ankle.

432
31:39.711 --> 31:40.545
I see.

433
31:46.926 --> 31:49.137
Aren't you going to ask how I got hurt?

434
31:51.139 --> 31:52.515
Are you hurt anywhere else?

435
31:52.598 --> 31:53.683
Yes.

436
31:54.517 --> 31:56.352
It hurts here too.

437
31:56.936 --> 31:59.105
I've got bruises everywhere.

438
31:59.689 --> 32:01.315
You're the ones who beat me up!

439
32:08.114 --> 32:10.658
I'll let the acupuncture needles sit

440
32:11.200 --> 32:12.660
for 20 minutes

441
32:12.744 --> 32:14.954
and come pull them out after checking on other patients.

442
32:15.038 --> 32:16.914
Give her an ointment for bruises too.

443
32:17.832 --> 32:19.584
It's fine. I have ointment at home.

444
32:20.418 --> 32:21.294
We'll take one.

445
32:22.253 --> 32:23.087
Just a moment.

446
32:33.264 --> 32:36.100
Doctor! Please help my son!

447
32:36.184 --> 32:37.852
Over here, Doctor!

448
32:37.935 --> 32:39.062
-Doctor! -Over here!

449
32:39.145 --> 32:42.356
-Doctor! -Please take a look at my boy, Doctor!

450
32:43.357 --> 32:44.650
What happened?

451
32:44.734 --> 32:45.735
Please take a look.

452
32:50.656 --> 32:53.993
"16-year-old girl honored with the governor-general's award."

453
32:54.077 --> 32:55.912
That's quite a nice drawing.

454
32:56.412 --> 32:58.664
But what does it have to do with anything?

455
32:58.748 --> 33:01.584
Well, the governor-general has always attended

456
33:01.667 --> 33:04.337
the Joseon Painting Exhibition himself to present the awards.

457
33:04.420 --> 33:06.881
But he's in Tokyo right now.

458
33:07.715 --> 33:09.675
Then who'll present the awards?

459
33:12.762 --> 33:14.347
The inspector general will.

460
33:14.889 --> 33:16.099
Exactly.

461
33:16.182 --> 33:19.769
The awards ceremony is at the Keijo Imperial University Library auditorium

462
33:19.852 --> 33:21.312
at 7:00 p.m. the day after tomorrow.

463
33:21.395 --> 33:24.816
The day after tomorrow is too soon.

464
33:24.899 --> 33:26.651
No, no.

465
33:26.734 --> 33:28.277
It's not impossible.

466
33:29.320 --> 33:31.197
We have to seize the opportunity when it comes.

467
33:31.697 --> 33:35.284
We still need to confirm if Sato will actually be there.

468
33:35.368 --> 33:37.453
Hold on. Who has the schedule?

469
33:37.537 --> 33:38.746
-Pass it over. -Okay.

470
33:39.747 --> 33:40.665
Look at the date.

471
33:43.334 --> 33:44.544
There it is, the speech.

472
33:45.419 --> 33:47.839
Sato will be at the awards ceremony.

473
33:47.922 --> 33:49.924
This is Sato's schedule she copied, isn't it?

474
33:50.007 --> 33:52.135
It says "speech" right here.

475
33:52.218 --> 33:54.220
When she first brought this to us,

476
33:54.303 --> 33:56.055
we couldn't exactly trust her.

477
33:56.139 --> 33:59.559
We had no idea what kind of speech he was giving or where.

478
33:59.642 --> 34:01.769
Now the same schedule is in the newspaper.

479
34:01.853 --> 34:03.771
What could be more certain than this?

480
34:05.982 --> 34:09.485
This is the first piece of intel from the girl you vouched for, So-ran.

481
34:09.569 --> 34:10.987
We're doing this, got it?

482
34:11.070 --> 34:12.655
-We're doing this, okay? -Okay.

483
34:12.738 --> 34:13.906
Well done.

484
34:13.990 --> 34:17.118
Listen, don't say anything to her.

485
34:17.201 --> 34:20.454
If she tips them off, we're in serious trouble.

486
34:24.000 --> 34:25.334
Sato.

487
34:25.418 --> 34:27.503
You'll be a dead man that day.

488
34:29.297 --> 34:30.381
Let's do this!

489
34:30.464 --> 34:31.299
Let's do it.

490
34:40.933 --> 34:42.351
What's taking him so long?

491
34:43.644 --> 34:45.479
We're nowhere near 20 minutes.

492
34:51.027 --> 34:52.528
I'm all better now.

493
34:52.612 --> 34:53.446
Ms. Keum.

494
34:54.572 --> 34:55.740
No.

495
34:55.823 --> 34:59.160
Why even bother coming here if you won't listen to the doctor?

496
34:59.243 --> 35:00.995
I never said I wanted to come.

497
35:04.040 --> 35:05.124
You can't just leave.

498
35:05.750 --> 35:08.878
We need to keep your ankle still. Sit down. I'll bandage it.

499
35:13.758 --> 35:15.426
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee.

500
35:15.509 --> 35:18.179
Don't you know what "strict hierarchical obedience"…

501
35:18.262 --> 35:19.931
Right, you don't know Chinese characters.

502
35:20.014 --> 35:22.266
No, I know that much.

503
35:22.350 --> 35:24.685
Then write it out in Chinese characters.

504
35:24.769 --> 35:26.062
If you can, you're free to go.

505
35:27.480 --> 35:28.397
Give me your palm.

506
35:29.607 --> 35:30.441
What?

507
35:30.524 --> 35:33.277
Give me your hand. You told me to write the characters.

508
35:36.155 --> 35:36.989
My hand…

509
35:39.367 --> 35:42.495
Sang, myeong, ha…

510
35:44.997 --> 35:45.831
bok.

511
35:46.624 --> 35:48.042
There, "Sangmyeonghabok."

512
35:49.460 --> 35:50.670
That "bok" is for the abdomen.

513
35:51.462 --> 35:52.296
What?

514
35:52.380 --> 35:55.383
The "bok" in the phrase means "to obey." But what you wrote

515
35:55.466 --> 35:56.300
means the "abdomen."

516
35:56.384 --> 35:58.135
I know.

517
35:58.219 --> 35:59.845
I got it mixed up for a moment.

518
36:00.554 --> 36:02.390
I'll write again. Give me your hand.

519
36:04.684 --> 36:06.060
There. Use that.

520
36:16.237 --> 36:17.071
Sang.

521
36:17.905 --> 36:19.156
Myeong.

522
36:19.865 --> 36:20.783
Ha.

523
36:57.486 --> 36:59.447
Do you know how to wrap a bandage?

524
37:00.489 --> 37:01.699
I learned it at school.

525
37:02.491 --> 37:03.576
At school?

526
37:05.119 --> 37:07.330
Do they teach you how to do this at school?

527
37:11.625 --> 37:13.669
I wouldn't know, I never went to school.

528
37:15.046 --> 37:16.672
When you enter the Army Academy,

529
37:16.756 --> 37:18.674
the first thing they teach you is first aid.

530
37:20.051 --> 37:20.926
Right.

531
37:21.510 --> 37:24.221
You graduated from the Imperial Japanese Army Academy.

532
37:36.692 --> 37:37.610
By the way,

533
37:38.194 --> 37:41.572
why did you become an interpreter instead of a soldier?

534
37:43.282 --> 37:44.116
All done.

535
37:45.368 --> 37:46.994
Get up and try walking.

536
37:49.747 --> 37:50.956
Okay.

537
37:59.131 --> 38:00.216
Is it feeling better?

538
38:01.592 --> 38:02.551
Yes.

539
38:09.350 --> 38:11.727
This is when you're supposed to say "thank you."

540
38:13.396 --> 38:14.897
Fine. Thank you.

541
38:16.440 --> 38:18.067
I'm not lying. I mean it.

542
38:20.903 --> 38:21.737
All right.

543
38:29.412 --> 38:30.913
About what you said yesterday.

544
38:31.622 --> 38:32.456
What?

545
38:33.958 --> 38:35.000
"I like you."

546
38:37.711 --> 38:39.213
You said yesterday

547
38:39.964 --> 38:41.132
that you liked me.

548
38:43.384 --> 38:45.428
You claimed you weren't lying.

549
38:50.057 --> 38:51.559
Don't let Mr. Yoo know.

550
38:54.645 --> 38:57.523
I need to keep things amicable with him.

551
38:59.567 --> 39:01.277
I hope you won't play dumb.

552
39:02.236 --> 39:04.530
You used that to join the Government-General.

553
39:06.240 --> 39:09.076
You said I was lying.

554
39:10.327 --> 39:12.371
You said you meant what you said.

555
39:16.417 --> 39:18.252
Of course, you were probably lying.

556
39:18.878 --> 39:21.130
But if, by any chance, you really meant it…

557
39:24.467 --> 39:26.177
don't let Mr. Yoo find out.

558
39:30.806 --> 39:31.849
Here you go.

559
39:31.932 --> 39:33.267
Thank you.

560
39:33.350 --> 39:36.645
DISPENSARY

561
39:40.566 --> 39:41.567
Here you go.

562
39:42.359 --> 39:44.361
Please wait. I'll go grab some ointment.

563
39:52.369 --> 39:54.788
Hold on to me. I don't mind.

564
39:55.998 --> 39:57.166
There's nowhere to sit.

565
40:00.544 --> 40:01.629
Thank you.

566
40:08.093 --> 40:09.136
Does he hit you?

567
40:10.346 --> 40:11.180
Sorry?

568
40:12.056 --> 40:14.767
Your wrists, the bruises, and ankles.

569
40:16.310 --> 40:17.728
Did he do that to you?

570
40:19.438 --> 40:20.648
Who are you talking…

571
40:24.235 --> 40:26.111
-No, it's not like that. -Seo-hee.

572
40:32.743 --> 40:34.119
It's you, Mr. Hideo.

573
40:35.913 --> 40:37.623
I wasn't sure it was you from behind.

574
40:45.005 --> 40:46.298
I didn't expect to see you here.

575
40:46.382 --> 40:47.341
Indeed.

576
40:49.635 --> 40:51.762
I'm here to get some medicine for my wife.

577
40:51.845 --> 40:54.390
I hear this is an excellent clinic.

578
40:55.015 --> 40:56.976
Is your wife still unwell?

579
40:57.059 --> 40:57.935
Yes.

580
40:58.686 --> 41:01.105
It seems it'll take some time for her to recover.

581
41:11.740 --> 41:15.244
Can Seo-hee go with me from here?

582
41:20.541 --> 41:22.084
Just today, if you don't mind.

583
41:25.713 --> 41:27.715
Yes. I'd appreciate it.

584
41:49.069 --> 41:51.989
It was nice seeing you today. Have a good day.

585
41:52.072 --> 41:52.948
Bye.

586
41:55.784 --> 41:57.578
Get your arm off me.

587
41:57.661 --> 42:00.372
We're lovers. What's the problem, honey?

588
42:04.877 --> 42:06.128
Son of a bitch.

589
42:06.712 --> 42:08.339
Still, this is a bit much.

590
42:08.422 --> 42:10.466
Sato Hideo is watching us.

591
42:14.678 --> 42:16.555
Why would she date a man like that?

592
42:31.028 --> 42:33.947
Did you think bringing him there would scare us?

593
42:34.031 --> 42:35.991
Why not just go ahead and tip them off?

594
42:36.075 --> 42:37.284
Look.

595
42:37.368 --> 42:39.745
I had no idea that was your den.

596
42:39.828 --> 42:41.205
I didn't bring him there.

597
42:41.288 --> 42:42.289
He's the one who…

598
42:44.750 --> 42:45.876
Just stay still.

599
42:58.180 --> 42:59.014
Mr. Yoo Philip.

600
43:07.439 --> 43:08.565
Mr. Hideo.

601
43:10.275 --> 43:11.902
I didn't think you'd catch us like this.

602
43:12.986 --> 43:14.196
What are you doing here?

603
43:14.780 --> 43:16.407
I thought you'd already left.

604
43:21.954 --> 43:23.122
The ointment.

605
43:23.205 --> 43:24.790
You should take it.

606
43:27.835 --> 43:28.669
Right.

607
43:29.294 --> 43:30.254
Thank you.

608
43:39.388 --> 43:40.639
So what you're saying is,

609
43:40.723 --> 43:43.726
you couldn't get around the building because your ankle hurt.

610
43:43.809 --> 43:45.602
That's why you found out nothing?

611
43:45.686 --> 43:46.562
Yes.

612
43:47.187 --> 43:49.732
On top of that, someone made me leave work early.

613
43:50.482 --> 43:53.485
How convenient. Now you have an excuse for your incompetence.

614
43:53.569 --> 43:54.737
What did you just say?

615
43:55.404 --> 43:57.656
Whose fault is it that I hurt my ankle?

616
43:59.032 --> 44:00.117
All right.

617
44:00.200 --> 44:03.454
I understand. It must've been hard getting around with your ankle.

618
44:04.246 --> 44:07.291
Watch how things go until you're better for the time being.

619
44:09.126 --> 44:10.502
Okay, I will.

620
44:15.340 --> 44:16.341
Good night.

621
44:18.719 --> 44:20.262
Read this.

622
44:21.847 --> 44:22.931
What is it?

623
44:23.599 --> 44:25.726
It's intel on the staff at the Government-General.

624
44:25.809 --> 44:27.853
The Satos aren't on it, but it should help.

625
44:30.564 --> 44:31.398
Okay.

626
44:33.734 --> 44:35.194
Who put this together?

627
44:39.406 --> 44:42.618
Have you ever had a spy inside the Government-General before?

628
44:42.701 --> 44:44.286
No, we haven't.

629
44:44.369 --> 44:46.663
We've been compiling this intel for a long time.

630
44:48.499 --> 44:49.333
Okay.

631
44:51.210 --> 44:52.920
-As for Sato Hideo-- -What?

632
44:57.508 --> 44:58.717
What about him?

633
45:00.177 --> 45:02.346
Did anything else happen at the clinic?

634
45:04.973 --> 45:06.183
"I like you."

635
45:09.019 --> 45:09.937
No.

636
45:10.938 --> 45:12.189
Nothing happened.

637
45:12.272 --> 45:13.273
Well…

638
45:13.816 --> 45:15.651
He took me to the clinic

639
45:15.734 --> 45:17.361
because he thinks I'm someone's lover.

640
45:17.444 --> 45:19.655
He was probably told to be nice to me.

641
45:23.200 --> 45:24.034
Right.

642
45:25.118 --> 45:25.953
Well then.

643
45:28.288 --> 45:29.248
Wait, Seo-hee.

644
45:37.464 --> 45:39.341
I'm sorry you got hurt.

645
45:45.681 --> 45:46.932
It's all right.

646
45:47.933 --> 45:50.936
I've been beaten worse. This is nothing.

647
45:54.106 --> 45:55.107
By the way,

648
45:55.732 --> 45:57.693
you two aren't really married, are you?

649
45:59.945 --> 46:01.655
But he likes you, doesn't he?

650
46:04.408 --> 46:07.077
I guess you've read popular fiction too much.

651
46:08.453 --> 46:10.038
I could tell from his eyes.

652
46:10.122 --> 46:12.040
He can't take his eyes off you.

653
46:12.124 --> 46:14.001
Married men aren't usually like that.

654
46:16.336 --> 46:17.421
But then…

655
46:18.505 --> 46:21.508
What about Seo-hee's father…

656
46:28.932 --> 46:31.476
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have brought it up.

657
46:35.147 --> 46:37.357
You don't like calling me Seo-hee,

658
46:38.317 --> 46:39.568
do you?

659
46:45.741 --> 46:49.244
Well, there's nothing we can do about it.

660
46:53.957 --> 46:54.833
All done.

661
46:55.334 --> 46:56.168
Get some sleep.

662
47:00.714 --> 47:02.257
Oh, I forgot one thing.

663
47:02.841 --> 47:04.718
According to the schedule you copied,

664
47:04.801 --> 47:08.430
Sato is supposed to give a speech at 7:00 p.m. Monday.

665
47:08.513 --> 47:10.933
Did you hear anything else about that schedule?

666
47:11.016 --> 47:12.059
A speech?

667
47:13.352 --> 47:14.353
There was that, huh?

668
47:14.436 --> 47:17.481
I was scrambling to copy the schedule.

669
47:18.065 --> 47:20.776
I didn't hear anything else about the speech.

670
47:22.653 --> 47:23.487
I see.

671
47:25.948 --> 47:27.157
Wait…

672
47:27.240 --> 47:28.909
The day after tomorrow is Monday, right?

673
47:29.993 --> 47:31.453
At 7:00 p.m…

674
47:31.536 --> 47:33.288
Making this book is so exhausting.

675
47:33.372 --> 47:37.250
Our chief has no pull, so other divisions get all the good time slots.

676
47:37.334 --> 47:40.045
Of all the times he could've picked, he chose that one?

677
47:40.128 --> 47:43.215
If we report to the inspector general at 7:00 p.m. the day after tomorrow,

678
47:43.298 --> 47:44.841
when are we supposed to go home?

679
47:46.134 --> 47:47.803
Enough dawdling!

680
47:47.886 --> 47:49.471
Get in here.

681
47:49.554 --> 47:50.889
Yes, coming!

682
47:51.932 --> 47:55.686
The Publications Division is working on a book about the history of Joseon.

683
47:55.769 --> 47:59.064
The briefing for the inspector general is at 7:00 p.m. the day after tomorrow.

684
47:59.648 --> 48:02.484
The Publications Division chief has no influence,

685
48:02.567 --> 48:04.945
so the other divisions took all the good slots

686
48:05.028 --> 48:06.863
and they're stuck with a late slot.

687
48:06.947 --> 48:08.865
The staff were grumbling about it.

688
48:09.533 --> 48:12.828
They said they'd never get home if the report started at 7:00 p.m.

689
48:14.705 --> 48:15.539
Are you sure?

690
48:16.748 --> 48:19.418
Yes. I overheard it when I was out on an errand.

691
48:19.501 --> 48:22.462
That's 7:00 p.m. on Monday.

692
48:22.546 --> 48:24.047
I suppose the inspector general

693
48:24.131 --> 48:26.800
has decided to spend the whole week getting briefings.

694
48:27.718 --> 48:28.760
Well, why do you ask?

695
48:30.387 --> 48:31.304
No, it's nothing.

696
48:31.888 --> 48:34.016
You look like you're doubting me.

697
48:34.891 --> 48:36.393
I earn my keep.

698
48:38.145 --> 48:40.022
I know. I trust you.

699
49:19.436 --> 49:20.312
No, wait.

700
49:20.854 --> 49:22.189
What do you mean?

701
49:23.982 --> 49:26.359
So, So-ran, you're saying

702
49:26.943 --> 49:30.697
Sato will be at the Government-General at the time of the ceremony tomorrow?

703
49:32.365 --> 49:33.909
-Did she tell you that? -Yes.

704
49:34.451 --> 49:35.368
At the same time,

705
49:35.452 --> 49:38.663
the Publications Division will give a briefing on the Joseon history project.

706
49:40.415 --> 49:42.918
The girl who won first place in the art competition

707
49:43.001 --> 49:45.754
said the inspector general was supposed to present the award.

708
49:46.588 --> 49:49.132
I confirmed it through the girl's mother.

709
49:49.216 --> 49:52.260
I looked into it, and she works at Joil Textile Factory.

710
49:52.344 --> 49:55.597
The school asked her parents to attend as the inspector general would come.

711
49:55.680 --> 49:58.266
I confirmed they'd requested a shift change at work.

712
49:58.350 --> 50:01.770
The Jongno Police Station was instructed to assign officers tomorrow

713
50:01.853 --> 50:05.023
because Sato will be attending the awards ceremony.

714
50:05.565 --> 50:07.901
I overheard the police talking while I was camping out

715
50:07.984 --> 50:09.820
at the udon shop near the police station.

716
50:10.487 --> 50:13.615
The Keijo Imperial University library, where the ceremony is being held,

717
50:13.698 --> 50:16.326
was told to prepare the VIP room in the auditorium.

718
50:16.409 --> 50:18.328
I confirmed it with a library cleaner.

719
50:18.411 --> 50:20.747
She's the one who copied the schedule.

720
50:20.831 --> 50:24.543
She said she overheard it, but she could have heard wrong.

721
50:24.626 --> 50:25.585
That's right.

722
50:26.711 --> 50:27.712
So-ran.

723
50:28.547 --> 50:31.466
We know she's quick with her hands and sharp,

724
50:32.217 --> 50:34.719
but in this situation, shouldn't you trust us?

725
50:53.488 --> 50:56.449
16-YEAR-OLD GIRL HONORED WITH THE GOVERNOR-GENERAL'S AWARD

726
51:02.038 --> 51:05.375
THE DAY OF THE OPERATION

727
51:32.611 --> 51:34.279
Do you have something to tell me?

728
51:35.530 --> 51:36.448
Well…

729
51:37.240 --> 51:39.576
You look quite busy today.

730
51:39.659 --> 51:42.204
You haven't left your desk since this morning.

731
51:42.287 --> 51:45.790
Are you preparing for the report to the inspector general?

732
51:45.874 --> 51:48.460
The chief reports for the Foreign Affairs Division.

733
51:48.543 --> 51:49.753
I'm just an interpreter.

734
51:52.172 --> 51:53.381
I see.

735
51:55.383 --> 51:58.386
How do you know about the briefing for the inspector general?

736
52:01.139 --> 52:02.599
I don't think I mentioned it.

737
52:04.142 --> 52:06.645
I overheard some people talking in the hallway.

738
52:11.441 --> 52:12.317
Ms. Keum.

739
52:13.235 --> 52:14.069
Yes?

740
52:14.736 --> 52:17.906
Try not to wander around the Government-General.

741
52:17.989 --> 52:19.241
People are watching.

742
52:19.783 --> 52:21.493
There aren't many female employees here.

743
52:22.202 --> 52:23.703
Okay, I understand.

744
52:26.206 --> 52:29.626
It's a beautiful day, isn't it?

745
52:52.274 --> 52:53.108
Next.

746
53:21.553 --> 53:22.846
WWP NEWS

747
54:02.802 --> 54:04.012
That's a wrap.

748
54:14.773 --> 54:17.650
DONGSUNG TEXTILES

749
54:24.866 --> 54:26.576
There's a second floor over the drapery shop.

750
54:27.243 --> 54:29.954
So-ran, wait there in ambush.

751
54:30.038 --> 54:34.376
If Sato goes from the Government-General to Keijo Imperial University,

752
54:34.459 --> 54:37.921
he has to go by Angukjeong and pass in front of Changdeokgung Palace.

753
54:38.004 --> 54:39.297
This is Ihwajeong.

754
54:39.381 --> 54:41.216
Farther down, it's a three-way intersection.

755
54:41.299 --> 54:42.550
There's a straight road here.

756
54:42.634 --> 54:44.677
If you take this one, it's a detour,

757
54:44.761 --> 54:46.638
but you can get to Keijo Imperial University.

758
54:46.721 --> 54:50.100
So we'll block this first route

759
54:50.183 --> 54:52.185
and make him take the second one.

760
54:52.268 --> 54:54.229
Once Sato takes this road,

761
54:54.312 --> 54:56.773
I'll follow him on a bicycle and shoot him.

762
54:57.524 --> 54:58.358
No.

763
54:58.942 --> 55:00.068
This time, I'll do it.

764
55:00.151 --> 55:03.488
So-ran and the two doctors here.

765
55:03.571 --> 55:05.115
They may already recognize you

766
55:05.198 --> 55:07.158
or run into you again someday.

767
55:07.242 --> 55:08.576
Cheol-yong, my friend.

768
55:08.660 --> 55:10.203
You're the most at risk.

769
55:10.286 --> 55:12.497
Your photos are posted all over Gyeongseong.

770
55:12.580 --> 55:15.583
Come on. That photo was taken so long ago.

771
55:15.667 --> 55:17.836
It doesn't look like me anymore, does it?

772
55:17.919 --> 55:20.630
Don't worry. I'll be fine with a hat on.

773
55:20.713 --> 55:23.716
Then I'll ride the bicycle.

774
55:25.760 --> 55:27.220
You've got three kids, right?

775
55:27.303 --> 55:28.847
Does your family know

776
55:28.930 --> 55:30.765
you do this outside the clinic?

777
55:30.849 --> 55:32.142
Not a clue.

778
55:32.225 --> 55:34.477
But if they find out, wouldn't they be proud?

779
55:34.561 --> 55:35.770
I should take the bike--

780
55:35.854 --> 55:36.855
Forget it.

781
55:36.938 --> 55:39.149
I was known as Uhm Bok-dong back in the day.

782
55:39.232 --> 55:40.191
I'll ride the bike.

783
55:40.275 --> 55:41.526
If you really want to,

784
55:42.235 --> 55:45.280
you can block this first route, okay?

785
55:45.363 --> 55:46.239
Okay.

786
55:55.707 --> 55:58.418
Detour! Turn around!

787
56:05.341 --> 56:07.510
What the hell are you doing?

788
56:07.594 --> 56:08.678
Oh my!

789
56:08.761 --> 56:09.721
Get it out of here!

790
56:09.804 --> 56:10.889
What a waste.

791
56:10.972 --> 56:13.183
-What the hell is this? -Yes, excuse me.

792
56:13.266 --> 56:15.477
What are they saying? I'm sorry.

793
56:15.560 --> 56:17.145
Clean it up already!

794
56:17.228 --> 56:19.814
Do you think I understand a word you're jabbering?

795
56:19.898 --> 56:21.608
It's your fault for blocking the path.

796
56:22.108 --> 56:23.109
Okay, excuse me.

797
56:37.165 --> 56:38.416
What floor are you going, sir?

798
56:47.884 --> 56:49.511
Why are you still here?

799
56:49.594 --> 56:50.762
You have nothing to do.

800
56:51.554 --> 56:53.431
You never told me to go home.

801
56:54.974 --> 56:56.100
You should go home.

802
56:56.726 --> 56:58.061
Okay, thank you.

803
56:59.354 --> 57:01.523
Bring me a photo of yourself by tomorrow.

804
57:01.606 --> 57:03.441
It's for your ID at the Government-General.

805
57:05.068 --> 57:06.819
My photo?

806
57:07.654 --> 57:08.530
Yes.

807
57:09.280 --> 57:10.740
Is there a problem?

808
57:11.366 --> 57:12.325
No.

809
57:12.408 --> 57:13.326
It's just…

810
57:13.409 --> 57:14.911
I don't have any photos.

811
57:18.206 --> 57:19.457
Then you can ask him

812
57:19.541 --> 57:22.085
to take your picture with the newspaper's camera.

813
57:24.254 --> 57:25.213
That will work.

814
57:34.097 --> 57:36.099
-See you tomorrow. -Have a good night.

815
57:42.272 --> 57:46.025
Sato is supposed to give a speech at 7:00 p.m. Monday.

816
57:46.109 --> 57:48.653
Did you hear anything else about that schedule?

817
57:48.736 --> 57:52.532
The briefing for the inspector general is at 7:00 p.m. the day after tomorrow.

818
57:59.455 --> 58:01.207
Publications Division, please.

819
58:03.960 --> 58:07.171
Hello, I'm Keum Seo-hee from the Foreign Affairs Division.

820
58:07.672 --> 58:11.050
Mr. Sato Hideo lent you the English dictionary.

821
58:11.134 --> 58:13.928
Could I come by around 7:00 p.m. to pick it up?

822
58:18.182 --> 58:19.017
All right.

823
58:27.400 --> 58:30.028
Hello? Yoo Philip from WWP News.

824
58:30.695 --> 58:31.529
It's me.

825
58:31.613 --> 58:33.448
Where are you calling from?

826
58:34.240 --> 58:35.074
What?

827
58:35.158 --> 58:37.076
I'm at the Government-General.

828
58:40.330 --> 58:42.248
Are you crazy? Calling me from there?

829
58:42.332 --> 58:44.500
I called your house, but no one answered.

830
58:45.335 --> 58:47.337
Why on earth did you call me?

831
58:49.505 --> 58:50.340
It's just…

832
58:51.174 --> 58:52.467
Never mind.

833
58:53.301 --> 58:54.260
Hang on.

834
59:16.199 --> 59:17.825
No questions. Did you forget?

835
59:20.870 --> 59:22.038
Wait…

836
59:25.958 --> 59:26.959
Unbelievable.

837
59:27.043 --> 59:28.753
I went out of my way to call him.

838
59:30.129 --> 59:32.006
I spoke to him in English

839
59:32.090 --> 59:34.842
so the operator wouldn't understand, but he didn't even thank me.

840
59:58.908 --> 01:00:01.119
I see you smelled something sweet.

841
01:00:01.202 --> 01:00:02.662
-Here. -Thank you.

842
01:00:03.746 --> 01:00:05.289
You want some too?

843
01:00:05.373 --> 01:00:07.291
I can't sell these anyway. Take it.

844
01:00:07.375 --> 01:00:08.334
Thank you.

845
01:00:08.418 --> 01:00:09.711
You should share it!

846
01:00:09.794 --> 01:00:11.754
-Give me some! -No.

847
01:00:11.838 --> 01:00:12.672
You too?

848
01:00:13.464 --> 01:00:15.299
He'll be here soon.

849
01:00:15.383 --> 01:00:17.760
Get this cleaned up. Hurry!

850
01:00:18.720 --> 01:00:19.721
Here.

851
01:00:19.804 --> 01:00:21.764
-Thank you. -Take it.

852
01:00:22.306 --> 01:00:23.891
I can't sell them anyway. Here.

853
01:00:23.975 --> 01:00:25.685
-Thank you. -You should share it.

854
01:00:29.188 --> 01:00:32.191
I'm not good at shooting from a distance.

855
01:00:32.275 --> 01:00:34.569
I'll get up against the car window and shoot.

856
01:00:34.652 --> 01:00:36.738
So-ran, you're great at both.

857
01:00:36.821 --> 01:00:38.948
So please let me have this one, okay?

858
01:00:40.324 --> 01:00:43.703
Come on, let me look cool for once, please?

859
01:00:43.786 --> 01:00:46.330
We're taking him down for sure this time! Okay?

860
01:00:46.414 --> 01:00:47.999
Let me get married

861
01:00:48.082 --> 01:00:49.333
before I turn 60.

862
01:01:27.705 --> 01:01:28.956
Got you.

863
01:02:38.943 --> 01:02:41.696
-Where are they shooting from? -Where did it come from?

864
01:03:52.183 --> 01:03:53.142
Are you all right?

865
01:03:59.023 --> 01:04:00.107
Get in!

866
01:04:02.860 --> 01:04:03.694
Let's go.

867
01:04:06.656 --> 01:04:08.658
Damn it. Get in!

868
01:04:17.917 --> 01:04:18.918
Get in!

869
01:04:34.225 --> 01:04:36.060
Jeong-yeop, stay awake.

870
01:04:36.143 --> 01:04:37.812
You have to stay awake.

871
01:04:38.688 --> 01:04:39.855
Wake up, you punk!

872
01:04:41.399 --> 01:04:43.401
Jeong-yeop!

873
01:04:51.575 --> 01:04:52.410
Chief!

874
01:05:11.303 --> 01:05:12.680
Over there!

875
01:05:13.431 --> 01:05:14.348
Over there!

876
01:06:32.885 --> 01:06:36.806
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

877
01:06:37.723 --> 01:06:38.891
Madam.

878
01:06:38.974 --> 01:06:40.684
After the shootout last night,

879
01:06:42.019 --> 01:06:44.230
we're hunting down the remaining fugitives.

880
01:06:45.231 --> 01:06:47.399
-Out of the office? -Orders from above.

881
01:06:47.483 --> 01:06:50.903
I was going to call for a Joseon language interpreter.

882
01:06:50.986 --> 01:06:52.279
I'd appreciate your help.

883
01:06:52.363 --> 01:06:54.031
Why are you using that name?

884
01:06:54.115 --> 01:06:55.074
Unless you want to…

885
01:06:55.157 --> 01:06:56.450
Please let me go.

886
01:06:56.534 --> 01:06:58.994
…watch your family die in front of you.

887
01:07:00.996 --> 01:07:02.164
I suppose…

888
01:07:02.248 --> 01:07:03.541
You people are insane!

889
01:07:04.250 --> 01:07:05.876
…this is where it ends.

890
01:07:14.885 --> 01:07:16.887
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
